## Stack

Next.js (App Router) · TypeScript strict · MongoDB via Mongoose ·
TanStack Query v5 · shadcn/ui · Tailwind CSS · Zod · Vitest · pnpm

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` — dev server
- `pnpm build` — production build (must pass before any PR)
- `pnpm test` — run tests
- `pnpm lint` / `pnpm typecheck` — lint and types

## Architecture

- `src/app/` — routes, layouts, route handlers. Thin: validate → call service.
- `src/modules/<feature>/` — feature code: `components/`, `services/`, `schemas/`,
  `actions.ts` (server actions), `keys.ts` + `queries.ts` + `mutations.ts`
  (TanStack Query factories). Services own all business logic and DB access.
- `src/components/ui/` — shadcn/ui components, CLI-generated
  (`pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name>`), composed by feature components.
- `src/lib/db/` — connection singleton (`connect.ts`) + Mongoose models (`models/`).
- `src/lib/query/get-query-client.ts` — the only place a QueryClient is created.
- `src/lib/env.ts` — Zod-validated env. Never import from client components.

## Rules

- All external input is Zod-validated before reaching a service.
- Services return plain DTOs (`.lean()` + explicit mapping) — never Mongoose docs.
- Every server action and route handler checks auth itself.
- Client components read server data through `useQuery`/`useSuspenseQuery` with
  a `queryOptions` factory — never `useEffect` + `fetch`. Query keys come from
  the module's `keys.ts` factory only.
- Every mutation invalidates its covering query-key prefix (`onSuccess`), plus
  `revalidatePath` when RSC-rendered data changed.
- Routes that render Query data prefetch on the server
  (`void queryClient.query(opts).catch(noop)` + `HydrationBoundary`).
- List queries are always paginated.
- Server components by default; `'use client'` on the smallest leaf that needs it.
- Every model file uses the `models.X ?? model('X', schema)` hot-reload guard.
- Conventional commits. No AI attribution or Co-Authored-By trailers, ever.

## Environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local`. Required: `MONGODB_URI`, `AUTH_SECRET`.
